## How this guide is organized

The guide moves from the basics to specialized topics, and each page can be read on its own once
the first few are familiar.

- **Getting started** covers installation and a [quick tour](quick-start.qmd) of the library.
- **Building graphs** explains the [graph model](graph-model.qmd), the
  [construction methods](building-graphs.qmd), [generators](generators.qmd), and the
  [bundled datasets](datasets.qmd).
- **Working with graphs** covers [node and edge data](node-and-edge-data.qmd),
  [selections](selections.qmd), [traversals](traversals.qmd), and
  [Cypher queries](cypher.qmd).
- **Analysis** works through the algorithm families, from
  [structural properties](structure.qmd) and [paths](paths.qmd) to
  [centrality](centrality.qmd), [communities](communities.qmd), and beyond.
- **Visualization** covers [static plots](plotting.qmd), [layouts](layouts.qmd),
  [aesthetics](aesthetics.qmd), [interactive widgets](interactive.qmd), and the
  [step log](step-log.qmd).
- **Interoperability** covers [file formats](file-formats.qmd),
  [other libraries](other-libraries.qmd), and [summary tables](tables.qmd).
- **Specialized topics** cover [multiplex networks](multiplex.qmd),
  [network biology](network-biology.qmd), and [spreading and robustness](spreading.qmd).

Each page links to the [API reference](../reference/index.qmd) for the methods it uses, where every
parameter is documented in full.
